sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: x402 failure: the facilitator is down or times out
  accDescr: Sequence diagram: x402 failure: the facilitator is down or times out. 4 participants: Client (agent), Resource server, Facilitator, and Base Sepolia. 5 steps, 3 crossing a trust boundary, 1 failure branch. Based on x402 v2.0 (2025-12-09). Step 1: Client (agent) to Resource server: Retry with PAYMENT-SIGNATURE. Step 2: Resource server to Facilitator: POST /verify (no answer). This step crosses a trust boundary. Step 3: Resource server to Client (agent): 502 Bad Gateway. Step 4: Resource server to Facilitator: POST /settle (times out). This step crosses a trust boundary. If The facilitator answers settlement_pending: Non-terminal. The response carries the broadcast hash the SDK server retries settle once, and the facilitator reconciles against that hash. Step 5: Resource server to Base Sepolia: Reconcile: look up the transaction. This step crosses a trust boundary.
  autonumber
  participant p_client as Client (agent)
  participant p_server as Resource server
  participant p_facilitator as Facilitator
  participant p_chain as Base Sepolia
  p_client->>p_server: Retry with PAYMENT-SIGNATURE
  p_server->>p_facilitator: POST /verify (no answer)
  Note over p_server,p_facilitator: Crosses a trust boundary
  p_server-->>p_client: 502 Bad Gateway
  alt Expected path
    p_server->>p_facilitator: POST /settle (times out)
    Note over p_server,p_facilitator: Crosses a trust boundary
  else The facilitator answers settlement_pending
    Note over p_server,p_facilitator: Non-terminal. The response carries the broadcast<br/>hash#59; the SDK server retries settle once, and<br/>the facilitator reconciles against that hash.
  end
  p_server->>p_chain: Reconcile: look up the transaction
  Note over p_server,p_chain: Crosses a trust boundary
